1
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:48,020
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,090 --> 00:01:50,759
[Episode 25]

3
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:07,500
How was it?

4
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,520
Good thing
I stepped in to help you just now,

5
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,860
otherwise Dad would have kept

6
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:12,860
scolding you for who knows how long.

7
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,490
You should give me a reward.

8
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:16,500
Not much.

9
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:17,460
Just 200.

10
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,800
Who knows if you were really helping me

11
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,600
or just having fun at my expense?

12
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,030
Yun Li.

13
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,460
You're biting the hand that feeds you.

14
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:28,000
If you're going to be like this,

15
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,360
I won't help you next time.

16
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,690
Are you threatening me?

17
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,560
Fine, then I'll tell everyone

18
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,890
about your secrets too.

19
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:34,620
I...

20
00:02:38,410 --> 00:02:39,400
Go tell them.

21
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,690
Go ahead and tell them.

22
00:02:40,690 --> 00:02:42,240
Dad will definitely say,

23
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,300
"Look at your brother, only 18,

24
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:43,930
and he already found

25
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:45,300
such a great girlfriend.

26
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:46,300
He's so charming.

27
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:47,360
What about you?"

28
00:02:49,590 --> 00:02:50,400
Li,

29
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:51,630
if you ask me,

30
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,430
you should just go meet him.

31
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:55,800
Don't be so opposed to blind dates.

32
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:58,500
What if you meet a good match?

33
00:02:58,500 --> 00:02:59,300
I'm not going.

34
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:03,250
Yun Ye, whose side are you on?

35
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,090
I'm on your side, of course.

36
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:07,090
But I... I just don't want

37
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:07,900
you and Dad

38
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:09,680
to keep fighting.

39
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:11,770
It's not good for family harmony.

40
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,190
Don't you agree?

41
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:22,329
Li,

42
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:24,630
your ex-boyfriend seems to be sick.

43
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:30,780
Do you want to go see him?

44
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:33,740
No.

45
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:35,250
It has

46
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:36,530
nothing to do with me.

47
00:03:47,030 --> 00:03:48,360
Is there anything else?

48
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,820
If not, stop sitting here.

49
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:53,340
I'm leaving.

50
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,300
200. Don't forget.

51
00:04:22,190 --> 00:04:23,000
Lili.

52
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,450
Why are you here?

53
00:04:35,330 --> 00:04:36,130
I...

54
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,000
It's Yun Ye.

55
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,659
He left a notebook

56
00:04:39,659 --> 00:04:40,930
in the lab.

57
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,600
I... I was on my way,

58
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,390
so I'm picking it up for him.

59
00:04:48,130 --> 00:04:49,260
I'll take you there.

60
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:51,180
Okay.

61
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:53,920
Let's go. This way.

62
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:11,040
The second desk

63
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,150
is Yun Ye's.

64
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:31,930
Yun Li, what are you doing?

65
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:33,920
You're being ridiculous.

66
00:05:36,890 --> 00:05:37,750
Did you find it?

67
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,300
N-Not yet.

68
00:05:40,159 --> 00:05:40,890
What does it look like?

69
00:05:40,890 --> 00:05:41,850
I'll help you look.

70
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:42,730
Never mind.

71
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:44,300
Maybe Yun Ye doesn't even know

72
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,690
where he put it.

73
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:48,190
I'm sorry

74
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,890
for making you bring me here.

75
00:05:51,450 --> 00:05:52,250
It's fine.

76
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,860
Are you sick?

77
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,130
Are you feeling unwell?

78
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:06,890
Insomnia.

79
00:06:10,130 --> 00:06:12,130
What did you think was wrong with me?

80
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:14,630
Nothing.

81
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,100
It's just... it's been so long,

82
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,960
and your insomnia is still so bad.

83
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:21,430
It doesn't happen every day.

84
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,040
It comes and goes.

85
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,190
I dream a lot.

86
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:39,659
If there's nothing else,

87
00:06:39,659 --> 00:06:40,920
I-I'll get going then.

88
00:06:41,130 --> 00:06:42,240
If you're not busy,

89
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,770
would you like to
come by my office for a while?

90
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:46,840
Oh, right.

91
00:06:46,850 --> 00:06:48,710
I happen to have a thesis template

92
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,830
that may be useful for Yun Ye.

93
00:06:49,830 --> 00:06:51,030
You can take it to him.

94
00:06:54,930 --> 00:06:56,060
I'll take you there.

95
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,220
First, open

96
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:18,190
that document from earlier.

97
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:19,220
Okay. This one?

98
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:20,190
Yes, this one.

99
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:20,870
Let me see.

100
00:07:20,890 --> 00:07:22,090
Just use this new one.

101
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,600
Everyone looks so busy.

102
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,190
Our daily life

103
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:29,190
is just like this.

104
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,190
Dormitory and lab.

105
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,500
See?

106
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:34,360
That's Senior's girlfriend.

107
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,460
She's the one I saw last time.

108
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:44,930
S-Sorry.

109
00:07:46,810 --> 00:07:47,810
Here's my office.

110
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,500
This is my office.

111
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:00,560
If you need me in the future,

112
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,740
you can come here.

113
00:08:15,190 --> 00:08:16,450
First, fold it in half.

114
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,060
Then,

115
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:20,420
fold this side to the center line.

116
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,240
You even know how to do this?

117
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,250
I'm a content creator.

118
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:24,660
I have to learn a lot of skills.

119
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:26,660
Tying knots, origami—

120
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:28,190
I know a lot of these things.

121
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,440
This side is the same.

122
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,150
Like this.

123
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:39,390
Then open it.

124
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,250
Like this.

125
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,100
Why does mine look

126
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,250
different from yours?

127
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:49,050
Yeah. Let me see.

128
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:51,980
It should be...

129
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:54,490
Why is it different? I must have...

130
00:08:58,820 --> 00:08:59,420
Like this?

131
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,600
Which way should it go?

132
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,800
Right, right.

133
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:09,390
Then...

134
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,420
D-Do the same on this side.

135
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,250
Fold it over.

136
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:35,790
Well?

137
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:38,500
Have I improved a lot?

138
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:49,780
I didn't expect you to still remember.

139
00:09:53,890 --> 00:09:56,670
You really have improved a lot.

140
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,500
I've been folding them often lately.

141
00:10:08,290 --> 00:10:10,090
And whenever I think of the past,

142
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:12,460
I unconsciously end up making

143
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:13,660
more and more of them.

144
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:24,460
Does it look good?

145
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,740
Yeah, pretty good.

146
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,030
It's for you.

147
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:40,440
If you like it,

148
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,090
you can take it back.

149
00:10:53,390 --> 00:10:54,180
Oh, right.

150
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:56,620
Please...

151
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,390
give this to Yun Ye.

152
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:15,440
It's getting late.

153
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:17,050
I'm heading back.

154
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:18,740
I'll walk you out.

155
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:20,580
Hurry! Let's go!

156
00:11:21,030 --> 00:11:21,650
Let's go!

157
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:58,500
She's the girl

158
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,160
on Senior's phone wallpaper.

159
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:02,240
So she's the wallpaper girl.

160
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,250
Is she the girl

161
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:04,630
Senior has had a crush on for a long time?

162
00:12:04,630 --> 00:12:05,600
Who knows?

163
00:12:06,770 --> 00:12:08,200
Do you think Senior

164
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,720
is pursuing her now?

165
00:12:09,910 --> 00:12:10,910
Looks like it.

166
00:12:14,010 --> 00:12:14,860
It's for you.

167
00:12:15,550 --> 00:12:16,500
Do you like it?

168
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:18,530
Take it if you like it.

169
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:24,240
He usually doesn't even let me touch

170
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:25,480
that paper lantern,

171
00:12:25,510 --> 00:12:26,620
and now he actually gave it away.

172
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:27,390
Seriously.

173
00:12:27,510 --> 00:12:28,960
It's one thing to give it away,

174
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,890
but he even said,

175
00:12:30,530 --> 00:12:33,070
"I... make them often."

176
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:39,400
Senior.

177
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:40,120
Senior.

178
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,720
Have you finished writing the report?

179
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,720
Yes, Senior.

180
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,390
I'll send it to you right away.

181
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:44,960
Let's go.

182
00:12:51,890 --> 00:12:52,700
Senior.

183
00:12:52,910 --> 00:12:54,200
Your way of pursuing someone

184
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,650
is too subtle.

185
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:57,510
She might not even know

186
00:12:57,510 --> 00:12:59,250
you're pursuing her.

187
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,920
Then what should I do?

188
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,410
Tell her how you feel about her directly.

189
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:07,340
Who could resist your confession?

190
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,860
Confession?

191
00:13:11,510 --> 00:13:12,460
If I do that now,

192
00:13:12,890 --> 00:13:14,550
she might delete me on WeChat.

193
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:17,940
Someone would actually delete you?

194
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,700
She deleted me twice.

195
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:27,150
Come on, Senior.

196
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:29,280
And you're still pursuing her?

197
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:30,250
Yes.

198
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:32,360
Yeah, Senior.

199
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:34,820
So many people are pursuing you.

200
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:36,360
There's no need to pursue someone

201
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,700
who deleted you twice.

202
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:39,250
She's so headstrong.

203
00:13:41,030 --> 00:13:41,840
Senior.

204
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:45,250
Are you a bit of a hopeless romantic?

205
00:13:50,890 --> 00:13:52,090
A hopeless romantic?

206
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:21,000
And the other side...

207
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:23,170
♪ I look up at the sky ♪

208
00:14:23,690 --> 00:14:26,340
♪ And there you are, always by my side ♪

209
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,550
♪ Since when did it begin? ♪

210
00:14:29,570 --> 00:14:32,770
♪ I can't quite recall ♪

211
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,500
You're kind of

212
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,000
interrupting my teaching.

213
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:33,790
Fu Shize.

214
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:36,770
♪ You became the clouds in my dreams ♪

215
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:37,790
Is origami important?

216
00:14:37,270 --> 00:14:39,430
♪ Silent and weightless ♪

217
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:42,730
♪ I wish I could stay ♪

218
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:46,500
♪ Walking by your side forever ♪

219
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:51,230
♪ Through seasons of endless change ♪

220
00:14:51,250 --> 00:14:53,410
♪ Through tides that ebb and flow ♪

221
00:14:55,210 --> 00:14:58,160
♪ Letting moments overlap ♪

222
00:14:58,190 --> 00:15:00,480
♪ As we feel the world transform ♪

223
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:05,190
♪ I'm just glad I was brave enough ♪

224
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:08,220
♪ To meet the moon ♪

225
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:11,170
♪ Gently, I pluck a piece of it ♪

226
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:14,090
♪ And let loneliness fade away ♪

227
00:15:14,110 --> 00:15:18,270
♪ I just wanna stay with you ♪

228
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,120
It's been so long.

229
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:21,470
♪ That's the only thing that matters ♪

230
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:25,240
♪ Love gives us all ♪

231
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:28,320
♪ Like the moon lighting up every night ♪

232
00:15:28,340 --> 00:15:29,160
♪ You know ♪

233
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:32,420
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

234
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:35,250
♪ No matter how many times I say
I love you ♪

235
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:38,850
♪ Clouds, please drift a little closer ♪

236
00:15:38,890 --> 00:15:42,100
By giving me this,
are you trying to say...

237
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:44,650
♪ I could say it ten thousand times
and never tire ♪

238
00:15:43,890 --> 00:15:45,720
you still miss me?

239
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:29,650
Change the bed sheets

240
00:16:29,650 --> 00:16:30,790
for the guest in room 209.

241
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:31,370
Okay.

242
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:46,860
Did you come here

243
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:48,320
to interfere with my work?

244
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:51,660
No.

245
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,390
I just missed you too much.

246
00:16:55,290 --> 00:16:57,410
Stop running over here every few days.

247
00:16:57,410 --> 00:16:58,810
Are flight tickets free?

248
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,330
Money is no big deal.

249
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:01,290
Think about it.

250
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:02,000
You're so pretty

251
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:02,930
and so charming.

252
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:03,600
What if someone

253
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,160
with similar good taste to mine

254
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,160
steals you away?

255
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:07,609
Then I'd be doomed.

256
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:10,520
You're such a smooth talker.

257
00:17:10,589 --> 00:17:11,310
Hurry up

258
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:12,510
and review your lessons.

259
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:14,660
Are you not gonna take
the postgraduate exam?

260
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:16,030
If you keep muddling along like this

261
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:17,030
and fail the exam,

262
00:17:17,089 --> 00:17:18,750
my dad will think
you are not good enough for me,

263
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:20,210
and we'll have to break up.

264
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,310
Don't.

265
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:22,710
Keep your voice down.

266
00:17:23,290 --> 00:17:24,750
I'll start reviewing tomorrow.

267
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:25,849
Tomorrow?

268
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:28,400
You should go back and study right away.

269
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:29,350
But look,

270
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,000
it's almost

271
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,220
lunch time.

272
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,150
You need to take a lunch break.

273
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:33,720
Let's go have lunch together.

274
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:34,980
All you know is eating.

275
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:37,810
I'm begging you.

276
00:17:37,810 --> 00:17:38,810
I rushed over here

277
00:17:38,810 --> 00:17:39,510
early this morning.

278
00:17:39,510 --> 00:17:40,510
I haven't had a single bite

279
00:17:40,510 --> 00:17:41,440
to eat until now.

280
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:42,290
Please.

281
00:17:44,590 --> 00:17:45,460
Fine.

282
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,100
Hurry back after eating.

283
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,530
So I'll book a table?

284
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:55,170
You've

285
00:17:55,190 --> 00:17:56,950
lost weight from working so much lately.

286
00:17:56,950 --> 00:17:58,710
You need more protein.

287
00:17:59,510 --> 00:18:00,440
This is good too.

288
00:18:00,810 --> 00:18:01,610
Try this.

289
00:18:05,610 --> 00:18:06,540
This is good too.

290
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:09,700
Lili!

291
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,530
So you invited Lili?

292
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,200
I haven't seen Lili
for a long time either.

293
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,510
If you have a problem with it,
you can leave.

294
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:17,770
I don't have a problem.

295
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,790
It's just that it's rare for us

296
00:18:18,790 --> 00:18:19,790
to have a chance to be alone, and...

297
00:18:19,790 --> 00:18:21,250
Don't talk too much later.

298
00:18:21,590 --> 00:18:22,400
Lili.

299
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:24,750
Lili.

300
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,550
Fu Zhengchu,

301
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:27,110
are you here to clock in again today?

302
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:28,920
I call this maintaining our relationship.

303
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:30,400
Otherwise, I'm afraid someone

304
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,800
will steal my Tangy away.

305
00:18:32,090 --> 00:18:33,460
Just eat.

306
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:36,610
I didn't dare to call you.

307
00:18:36,610 --> 00:18:38,090
I was afraid you were too busy.

308
00:18:38,090 --> 00:18:38,920
Whenever you want to see me,

309
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:39,850
I'm always free.

310
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:41,760
What about me?

311
00:18:42,790 --> 00:18:43,720
Why do you have to get
involved in everything?

312
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:44,290
Eat up.

313
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,490
Go home after eating.

314
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,500
Oh, right. Lili.

315
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,590
Tangy told me

316
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,090
that Yun Ye's teaching assistant

317
00:18:55,090 --> 00:18:55,960
is my uncle.

318
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:57,310
Have you guys

319
00:18:57,310 --> 00:18:58,250
met yet?

320
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,290
You're full, right? Hurry up and leave.

321
00:19:02,290 --> 00:19:03,200
But I haven't even started eating.

322
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:03,900
Get going.

323
00:19:05,630 --> 00:19:07,090
Then... Then I'll...

324
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:08,220
I'll get going then.

325
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:09,220
Bye-bye.

326
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,050
Bye-bye.

327
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,350
Why did you chase him away?

328
00:19:14,350 --> 00:19:15,680
He has a flight to catch.

329
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:16,560
Catch a flight?

330
00:19:31,290 --> 00:19:32,090
Tangy,

331
00:19:32,550 --> 00:19:33,350
um...

332
00:19:34,110 --> 00:19:35,000
A few days ago,

333
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,460
Fu Shize

334
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:41,200
gave me a paper lantern.

335
00:19:41,710 --> 00:19:42,590
A paper lantern?

336
00:19:42,590 --> 00:19:43,400
What's that?

337
00:19:45,290 --> 00:19:47,290
I taught him how to fold them before.

338
00:19:47,750 --> 00:19:49,750
He said whenever he thinks of the past,

339
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:51,280
he can't stop folding them.

340
00:19:51,550 --> 00:19:52,700
What does he want?

341
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:55,050
Does he want
to get back together with you?

342
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:56,630
I don't know.

343
00:19:57,050 --> 00:19:57,810
You know how much

344
00:19:57,810 --> 00:19:59,010
he put you through,

345
00:19:59,010 --> 00:19:59,960
right?

346
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:03,960
I know.

347
00:20:04,290 --> 00:20:05,750
You'd better really know.

348
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:26,610
Yun Ye.

349
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:29,000
Are you...

350
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:31,780
feeling better?

351
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,310
I'm fine.

352
00:20:43,090 --> 00:20:43,900
Yun Ye.

353
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:48,960
Never mind.

354
00:20:55,010 --> 00:20:55,790
Do you think your sister and I

355
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:56,920
still have a chance?

356
00:21:00,510 --> 00:21:02,270
Yun Ye, come in and change your dressing.

357
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:02,800
Okay.

358
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:04,250
I'm going in.

359
00:21:16,590 --> 00:21:17,720
Is Yun Ye okay?

360
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:19,550
He's fine.

361
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:20,900
He just got bitten by a bug

362
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:22,830
and went to put some medicine on it.

363
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:24,680
Okay, I'll go check on him.

364
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:30,960
Yun Ye.

365
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:32,090
Li.

366
00:21:32,110 --> 00:21:32,920
Let me see.

367
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:34,550
It's nothing.

368
00:21:36,010 --> 00:21:36,790
You're a grown man.

369
00:21:36,790 --> 00:21:37,790
How did you get bitten by a bug?

370
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:39,790
Can't you give us some peace of mind?

371
00:21:40,010 --> 00:21:41,290
I'm already like this.

372
00:21:41,290 --> 00:21:43,140
Stop nagging me.

373
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,420
Mom and Dad called me

374
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:47,020
and asked me to take you back.

375
00:21:47,020 --> 00:21:47,900
They heard you got bitten

376
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:48,890
by some unknown bug

377
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:49,560
and were so worried.

378
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:51,530
They have to see you with their own eyes
to put their minds at ease.

379
00:21:51,530 --> 00:21:53,460
Li, can you talk to Mom and Dad?

380
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:55,110
Ever since the surgery,

381
00:21:55,110 --> 00:21:56,310
they've been a bit...

382
00:21:58,810 --> 00:22:00,400
a bit too overprotective.

383
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:01,400
The hospital issued a notice

384
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,310
saying you were in critical condition.

385
00:22:03,310 --> 00:22:04,110
In their eyes,

386
00:22:04,110 --> 00:22:05,000
you have a bad track record.

387
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,730
I can't talk to them about this.

388
00:22:07,290 --> 00:22:08,090
Fine.

389
00:22:14,310 --> 00:22:16,590
Reporting the situation to Yunyi?

390
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,260
None of your business.

391
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:23,160
Looks like she didn't

392
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,810
come to the hospital with you.

393
00:22:24,810 --> 00:22:26,250
I didn't tell her.

394
00:22:27,590 --> 00:22:28,220
To be honest,

395
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:29,880
it doesn't look that serious.

396
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,060
It's one thing you didn't tell Yunyi,

397
00:22:32,270 --> 00:22:33,270
but why did you...

398
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:38,580
He insisted on bringing me here.

399
00:22:39,180 --> 00:22:40,290
Maybe...

400
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,330
he wanted to see you?

401
00:22:42,590 --> 00:22:44,320
Could you please wait outside?

402
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:59,010
Thank you for bringing

403
00:22:59,090 --> 00:23:00,690
Yun Ye to the hospital today.

404
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:03,450
I had nothing else to do anyway.

405
00:23:03,510 --> 00:23:05,440
Don't you need to go back to school?

406
00:23:06,050 --> 00:23:06,850
No.

407
00:23:10,510 --> 00:23:11,720
I'll keep you company while you're

408
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:12,650
waiting for him.

409
00:23:21,050 --> 00:23:21,850
Have a seat.

410
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:23,440
Okay.

411
00:24:21,550 --> 00:24:22,350
Um...

412
00:24:22,490 --> 00:24:23,860
Is... your

413
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:26,660
stomach... feeling better now?

414
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:28,460
Yeah.

415
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:34,220
I had surgery.

416
00:24:37,590 --> 00:24:38,590
What surgery?

417
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:40,570
Surgery for a perforated stomach.

418
00:24:40,570 --> 00:24:42,280
What? That serious?

419
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:44,660
When did you have the surgery?

420
00:24:48,090 --> 00:24:48,900
Last year.

421
00:24:50,790 --> 00:24:51,590
Last year?

422
00:24:54,930 --> 00:24:55,950
I don't remember

423
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,500
the exact time.

424
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,190
Was it March?

425
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:03,790
No.

426
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:06,160
The second half of last year, I think.

427
00:25:10,660 --> 00:25:12,160
You have stomach problems.

428
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,460
You need to eat regularly.

429
00:25:13,460 --> 00:25:14,350
Don't eat anything too hot

430
00:25:14,350 --> 00:25:15,790
or too cold.

431
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,640
And stop drinking coffee.

432
00:25:20,310 --> 00:25:20,900
Okay.

433
00:25:21,530 --> 00:25:24,010
And you definitely
shouldn't drink alcohol.

434
00:25:24,010 --> 00:25:25,740
I quit drinking a long time ago.

435
00:25:26,700 --> 00:25:27,420
Also...

436
00:25:27,420 --> 00:25:28,090
Li.

437
00:25:29,330 --> 00:25:30,000
I'm done.

438
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,530
The wound has been treated?

439
00:25:35,290 --> 00:25:36,090
Alright.

440
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:37,550
Thank you.

441
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,780
I'll treat you to a meal when I'm free.

442
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,200
Sure.

443
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:45,160
When will you be free?

444
00:25:49,660 --> 00:25:53,010
I'll... let you know later.

445
00:25:56,960 --> 00:25:57,750
Yun Ye.

446
00:25:58,310 --> 00:25:59,870
Get some rest when you go back.

447
00:25:59,870 --> 00:26:01,550
If there's anything
you don't understand in class,

448
00:26:01,550 --> 00:26:02,590
you can talk to me anytime.

449
00:26:02,590 --> 00:26:03,250
Okay.

450
00:26:05,350 --> 00:26:06,200
Say thank you.

451
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:08,270
Thank you.

452
00:26:08,310 --> 00:26:09,250
Thank you, sir.

453
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:10,200
Take care.

454
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:10,850
Okay.

455
00:26:39,810 --> 00:26:40,610
Li.

456
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:43,200
I have a gift for you.

457
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:44,220
What is it?

458
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:45,940
I managed to get a ticket

459
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:47,480
for N27 Band's concert.

460
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:49,180
They're only playing one show in Xifu.

461
00:26:49,180 --> 00:26:51,090
It sold out instantly when tickets
went on sale this weekend.

462
00:26:51,090 --> 00:26:51,810
It's yours.

463
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:54,050
You only got one ticket,

464
00:26:54,050 --> 00:26:55,610
so you couldn't go

465
00:26:55,610 --> 00:26:56,160
with your YY,

466
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:56,750
and you didn't want

467
00:26:56,750 --> 00:26:57,510
to go alone,

468
00:26:57,510 --> 00:26:58,750
so you're giving it to me, right?

469
00:26:58,750 --> 00:26:59,720
Come on. Why do you

470
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:00,660
overthink everything?

471
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:02,350
I just want to be nice to you.

472
00:27:02,350 --> 00:27:03,290
Is that wrong?

473
00:27:03,850 --> 00:27:04,660
No.

474
00:27:05,330 --> 00:27:06,130
Do you want it?

475
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:07,680
Totally.

476
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:08,720
Thanks.

477
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:10,310
Give me 200.

478
00:27:11,250 --> 00:27:12,350
I knew you were...

479
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:32,720
You want to go with me?

480
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:33,810
No.

481
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,750
Yun Ye got a ticket.

482
00:27:36,010 --> 00:27:38,340
I want to give it to you
as a thank-you gift.

483
00:27:40,810 --> 00:27:42,380
No need. Thanks.

484
00:27:45,810 --> 00:27:48,140
It seems this ticket
wasn't that hard to get.

485
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:49,600
Yun Ye was bragging again.

486
00:27:55,570 --> 00:27:56,830
What should I give him?

487
00:28:05,050 --> 00:28:05,850
You're here.

488
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:08,200
It's really hard to see you.

489
00:28:10,050 --> 00:28:11,450
How have you been lately?

490
00:28:13,660 --> 00:28:14,350
It seems like you say

491
00:28:14,350 --> 00:28:15,810
the same thing every time.

492
00:28:15,810 --> 00:28:16,510
It's like you're an AI

493
00:28:16,510 --> 00:28:17,840
programmed to say that.

494
00:28:18,610 --> 00:28:20,050
I just care about you.

495
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,400
Is your insomnia better?

496
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:24,860
I'm taking medicine.

497
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:27,000
I've been in Xifu

498
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:27,960
for so many days,

499
00:28:28,460 --> 00:28:30,290
but I haven't been able
to meet up with you.

500
00:28:30,290 --> 00:28:31,110
What made you want

501
00:28:31,110 --> 00:28:32,440
to meet up with me today?

502
00:28:39,550 --> 00:28:40,350
Tonight?

503
00:28:42,790 --> 00:28:43,850
Who did you ask out?

504
00:28:43,850 --> 00:28:44,610
You.

505
00:28:45,660 --> 00:28:47,030
How come I didn't know?

506
00:28:51,310 --> 00:28:52,850
Yun Li should be going too.

507
00:28:54,290 --> 00:28:55,090
Yun Li?

508
00:28:56,250 --> 00:28:58,180
She also has a ticket for this show.

509
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:01,960
I see.

510
00:29:02,810 --> 00:29:03,850
You want me to go with you

511
00:29:03,850 --> 00:29:05,160
to be your wingman.

512
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:07,550
I'm best at this.

513
00:29:08,590 --> 00:29:10,250
We're just watching the show.

514
00:29:10,250 --> 00:29:12,110
I'm not asking you to do anything.

515
00:29:14,750 --> 00:29:16,090
Just watching the show?

516
00:29:19,010 --> 00:29:20,160
Since when did you

517
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:21,590
like rock and roll?

518
00:29:26,220 --> 00:29:27,960
I wonder who said before

519
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:29,790
that he would finish his studies

520
00:29:29,790 --> 00:29:31,120
before looking for her.

521
00:29:32,850 --> 00:29:33,790
We just

522
00:29:34,350 --> 00:29:36,500
happened to run into each other.

523
00:29:40,510 --> 00:29:42,440
What was her attitude towards you?

524
00:29:43,940 --> 00:29:44,960
She...

525
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,200
Let's go.

526
00:29:52,790 --> 00:29:53,790
It's almost time.

527
00:29:55,250 --> 00:29:56,050
Come on.

528
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:57,250
What time is it?

529
00:29:57,250 --> 00:29:58,420
It's too early to go.

530
00:29:58,420 --> 00:29:59,820
It's not early. Let's go.

531
00:30:17,290 --> 00:30:17,810
Thanks.

532
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:24,960
We came so early

533
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:26,440
just to wait for her here?

534
00:30:29,350 --> 00:30:31,610
Why didn't you just ask her out directly?

535
00:30:32,290 --> 00:30:34,020
If I had asked her out directly,

536
00:30:35,050 --> 00:30:36,580
I might have been rejected.

537
00:30:36,920 --> 00:30:38,450
Aren't you going to tell me?

538
00:30:39,220 --> 00:30:40,310
Tell you what?

539
00:30:40,700 --> 00:30:41,350
Does she know

540
00:30:41,350 --> 00:30:43,480
you want to get back together with her?

541
00:30:45,460 --> 00:30:47,260
She...

542
00:30:48,510 --> 00:30:49,840
probably doesn't know.

543
00:30:59,910 --> 00:31:03,840
[The Magic of Light and Shadow:
A Vintage Camera Review]

544
00:31:20,510 --> 00:31:21,310
The author clearly lays out

545
00:31:21,310 --> 00:31:22,500
the evolution and development

546
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:23,660
of the technology

547
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:26,940
and offers some unique insights as well.

548
00:31:32,010 --> 00:31:33,400
We didn't wait in vain.

549
00:31:33,790 --> 00:31:34,850
The target is here.

550
00:31:41,660 --> 00:31:42,350
Yun Li?

551
00:31:43,550 --> 00:31:44,660
Long time no see.

552
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:50,890
Long time no see, Mr. Xu.

553
00:31:53,790 --> 00:31:54,850
Did you come alone?

554
00:31:56,180 --> 00:31:56,940
Mm-hmm.

555
00:32:01,220 --> 00:32:03,070
Come on. Let's go in together.

556
00:32:04,810 --> 00:32:05,570
Okay.

557
00:32:16,620 --> 00:32:18,820
♪ Let the music lead us ♪

558
00:32:19,040 --> 00:32:21,580
♪ To where we want to go ♪

559
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:24,080
♪ Let the sound waves guide us ♪

560
00:32:24,180 --> 00:32:26,830
♪ In this glowing show ♪

561
